CHAPTER.VERS:
Then I said to them, You

          {+}
         see the evil case that we are in, how Jerusalem lies waste, and its gates are burned with fire: come, and let us build up the wall of Jerusalem, that we will no more be a reproach.

But when Sanballat the Horonite, and Tobiah the slave, the Ammonite, and Geshem the Arabian, heard it, they laughed us to scorn, and despised us, and said, What is this thing that you

          {+}
         do? Will you

          {+}
         rebel against the king?

Then I answered them, and said to them, The God of heaven, he will prosper us; therefore we his slaves will arise and build: but you

          {+}
         have no portion, nor right, nor memorial, in Jerusalem.
